sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch13-06> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "If the maximal and minimal growth rates around the basal growth zone of a horn lie diametrically opposite, the horn is a plane spiral; otherwise it is a spiral in space with a helical component, which is the usual case because the horn's field of force has no such plane of symmetry.";
    dc:type "mathematical-law";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "A horn is a plane spiral only if fastest and slowest growth lie diametrically opposite";
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "plane spiral iff the maximal and minimal growth rates around the base lie at \\Delta\\phi = 180^\\circ; otherwise helicospiral";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "D’Arcy Wentworth Thompson, On Growth and Form (1st ed., Cambridge: Cambridge University Press, 1917), Chapter XIII, “The Shapes of Horns, and of Teeth or Tusks: with a Note on Torsion”; topic “Summary of horn growth”. Scope: horns of ruminants"
}
